Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.07,0:00:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Y measurements of a couple of the games.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.13,0:00:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,That's symmetric.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.31,0:00:16.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Yuuuu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.35,0:00:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Thinking I kill me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.69,0:00:22.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You realize what I'm doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.21,0:00:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Is the trouble?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.87,0:00:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.81,0:01:05.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So far, all of the evidence\Npoints to your defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.07,0:01:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I find you guilty of\Npoor dueling. Oh, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.55,0:01:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll just see. My move.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.23,0:01:13.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, what to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.09,0:01:18.57,Default,,0,0,0,,His face-down card is probably a trap,\Nbut I can't worry about that right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.65,0:01:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to get a monster on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.67,0:01:23.45,Default,,0,0,0,,or else he'll be able to\Nattack my life points again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.53,0:01:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,And I got just a guy for the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.01,0:01:27.45,Default,,0,0,0,,So look out, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.91,0:01:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I play this card.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.57,0:01:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Panther Warrior in attack mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.99,0:01:38.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And then, I'll place one card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.37,0:01:41.33,Default,,0,0,0,,His Cameon Wizard has\Nonly 1,300 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.47,0:01:44.75,Default,,0,0,0,,so my Panther Warrior should be\Nable to wipe it out with no problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.83,0:01:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,But just in case he tries anything funny,\NI've got my face down card as a backup.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.89,0:01:51.31,Default,,0,0,0,,That's it for me, Judge.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.65,0:01:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, you're up to something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.59,0:01:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh well, I'm not too worried.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.25,0:01:58.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I have this card.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.11,0:01:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Ready, Joseph?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.67,0:02:02.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Reveal the magic card leading question!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.67,0:02:05.87,Default,,0,0,0,,This card adds 800 attack\Npoints to any monster
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.95,0:02:08.73,Default,,0,0,0,,that's made up of two other\Nmonsters fused together.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.81,0:02:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,So my cameon, Wizard, is now\Nstronger than your panther warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.27,0:02:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Wizard, attack now!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.41,0:02:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.17,0:02:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Tall, Dark and Gruesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.01,0:02:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You've triggered my Trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.23,0:02:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Skull Dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.71,0:02:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The higher I roll, the more\Nattack points your monster loses.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.73,0:02:30.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.15,0:02:34.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps he should take a closer look.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.75,0:02:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.66,0:02:37.49,Default,,0,0,0,,A one?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.61,0:02:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.21,0:02:41.13,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.37,0:02:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know how you did\Nthat, but I got my eye on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.89,0:02:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,In my courtroom, twisting the facts is\Nperfectly legal, especially when it helps me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.17,0:02:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.21,0:02:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,My Panther Warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.47,0:02:57.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again, you have no\Nmonsters on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.29,0:03:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And as for me, you remember my\NSinister Justice card, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.67,0:03:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It gives me another 800 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.89,0:03:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Not again!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.43,0:03:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,That will happen every time my cameon\Nwizard attacks your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.65,0:03:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop this guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.89,0:03:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You almost had him beat once!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.09,0:03:17.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Until he turned things\Naround and whooped ya.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.89,0:03:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Gee, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.81,0:03:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Order in the court.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.67,0:03:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Make your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.37,0:03:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Jansen's got me right where he wants me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.39,0:03:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to his leading question magic card,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.77,0:03:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,his Cameon Wizard gets a\Npower boost of 800 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.87,0:03:32.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That gives it a grand total\Nof 2100 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.15,0:03:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And all I have in my hand is\Nthe Swordsman of Landstar.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.47,0:03:40.47,Default,,0,0,0,,who's not exactly what I'd\Ncall a king of monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.21,0:03:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.57,0:03:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Did little Joseph use up\Nall of his best monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.21,0:03:48.01,Default,,0,0,0,,during the first five\Nminutes of the duel? No!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.45,0:03:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The truth is, I did, and\Nnow I'm paying the price.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.15,0:03:54.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, make your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.17,0:03:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, fine, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.69,0:03:59.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, graceful dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.01,0:04:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,If my luck improves,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.59,0:04:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I may be able to raise my Swordsman\Nof Landstar's attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.79,0:04:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon Swordsman of Landstar!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.71,0:04:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,And then, I'll play\Nthis, my graceful dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.11,0:04:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, raise my sorceress\Nattack points with a high roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.57,0:04:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, it worked.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.27,0:04:24.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Not quite.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.61,0:04:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,What did I do to deserve all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.91,0:04:37.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I've never seen him have such\Nterrible luck before. Poor Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.39,0:04:42.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Joseph, that's my move now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.31,0:04:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to clear the\Ncourtroom of your monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.57,0:04:47.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Deck Master's special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.89,0:04:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, for the mere price of 1,000 life\Npoints, I've left you defenseless.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.13,0:04:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,The verdict is in.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.07,0:04:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You're finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.23,0:05:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,This case is coming to a close.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.03,0:05:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not over yet, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.59,0:05:07.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I've placed two cards face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.55,0:05:08.51,Default,,0,0,0,,So you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.83,0:05:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Now...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.74,0:05:11.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.13,0:05:16.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I play my plot of greed card.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.85,0:05:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet you wish you'd drawn\Nthis card, don't you, Joseph?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.13,0:05:22.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.04,0:05:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm able to draw two new cards,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.31,0:05:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,which is something that you\Nneed to do quite desperately.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.45,0:05:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, I can draw five cards now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.25,0:05:35.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I activate gamble!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.15,0:05:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You see,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.15,0:05:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no cards and you have six,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.07,0:05:45.69,Default,,0,0,0,,which is exactly the combination I needed\Nin order to activate this trap card.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.25,0:05:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Gamble?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.11,0:05:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.02,0:05:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a risky card, Taya.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.53,0:05:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,But if it works, it can help Joey\Nturn this entire duel around,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.79,0:05:55.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and it starts with a coin.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.19,0:05:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And what exactly is so\Nrisky about it, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.21,0:06:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Joey flips a coin in the air.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.67,0:06:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he calls heads or tails, and if\Nhe's right, he gets to draw five cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.03,0:06:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.94,0:06:07.03,Default,,0,0,0,,But if he's wrong,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.49,0:06:11.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's next turn gets skipped, And\Nhe can't afford to let that happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.21,0:06:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It could cost him the entire duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.29,0:06:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,He can take all the risks he wants,\Nbecause in my virtual courtroom,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.21,0:06:20.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I control everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.61,0:06:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.59,0:06:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,This could make or break the game for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.49,0:06:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe this door will lead us back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.01,0:06:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess not.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.47,0:06:39.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh. Oh, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.75,0:06:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,At least it's a change of scenery.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.95,0:06:42.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.19,0:06:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't want to be on a virtual beach,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.09,0:06:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,in a virtual forest, or even\Nin a virtual amusement park!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.21,0:06:49.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I want out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.51,0:06:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, Seto.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.67,0:06:53.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I just have to get that off my chest.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.67,0:06:56.61,Default,,0,0,0,,This place is really\Ngetting to me. Just relax.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.01,0:07:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,If you get upset, then\Nyou're letting Noah win. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.89,0:07:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Noah, show yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.87,0:07:05.27,Default,,0,0,0,,We're on to your little\Ngame and it won't work!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.35,0:07:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you can wear us down\Nby toying with our emotions,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.09,0:07:12.67,Default,,0,0,0,,but you obviously don't know\Nwho you're dealing with Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.17,0:07:19.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd say I know exactly who I'm dealing\Nwith Seto a no-good thief Now where was I?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.01,0:07:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.97,0:07:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Joey. You can do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.21,0:07:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You have a 50-50 chance
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.37,0:07:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Not exactly
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.47,0:07:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It's heads.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.21,0:07:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.35,0:07:36.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.13,0:07:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,No, not again.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.27,0:07:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This is bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.87,0:07:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,When is this poor fool going to learn\Nthat as long as we're in my courtroom,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.61,0:07:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I control the outcome?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.75,0:07:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It's still my turn, so I'll\Nreveal my face-down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.11,0:07:54.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Scapegoat!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.91,0:08:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Are those furballs\Nsupposed to frighten me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.89,0:08:03.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll have them dismissed\Nfrom this trial in no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.71,0:08:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,This ought to do for starters.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.23,0:08:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll play my Reinforcement\Nof the Army Magic Card first.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.51,0:08:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,allowing me to add a warrior to my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.55,0:08:16.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll use polymerization.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.71,0:08:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Know why, Joseph?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.19,0:08:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,To fuse together my R-Mail warrior\Nand my one-eyed shield dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.67,0:08:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Meet Dragoness, the Wicked Knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.77,0:08:30.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, big deal, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.11,0:08:32.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Your monster looks weak to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.23,0:08:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But wait, thanks to\Nthat magic card of his,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.13,0:08:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Johnson can increase the\Nattack points of any monster
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.79,0:08:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,that's made up of two other\Nmonsters fused together.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.65,0:08:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Time for my leading question\Nmagic card to kick in.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.55,0:08:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And power up my cameon wizard as\Nit tears down your first scapegoat.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.53,0:08:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it will increase the\Nstrength of my wicked
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.25,0:08:58.99,Default,,0,0,0,,knight as it eliminates\Nyour second scapegoat.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.81,0:09:07.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Two down, and two more scapegoats left.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.71,0:09:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Not if I stop you first.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.07,0:09:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Objection.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.07,0:09:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Your turn is skipped.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.83,0:09:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You called heads, but\Nyou got tails, Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.01,0:09:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, then go.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.61,0:09:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.25,0:09:22.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, time to destroy one more scapegoat.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.87,0:09:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And last but not least,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.11,0:09:30.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll enhance the strength\Nof my wicked knight
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.27,0:09:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,once more and dismiss your last scapegoat.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.39,0:09:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I'm done for.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.31,0:09:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Case closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.81,0:09:42.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you admit defeat? No.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.99,0:09:47.19,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel won't be over until your\Nlife points reach zero, Jansen.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.51,0:09:49.15,Default,,0,0,0,,No way am I giving up.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.93,0:09:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Ow.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.05,0:09:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Note to self, do not\Npunch virtual railing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.65,0:09:55.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.65,0:09:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't give up, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.79,0:10:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,This bad luck of yours is bound to\Nchange Because it can't get any worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.93,0:10:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Taya, listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.17,0:10:07.17,Default,,0,0,0,,As far as pep talks go,\Nthis is not your best work.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.29,0:10:09.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm running out of options here.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.67,0:10:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't give up!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.93,0:10:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,There's something fishy\Nabout this Johnson guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.85,0:10:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems like more than just bad\Nluck that's holding Joey down.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.97,0:10:19.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Yugi, I agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.27,0:10:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Much more.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.39,0:10:24.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Johnson is controlling the\Noutcome of Joey's moves.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.31,0:10:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been sensing it since\Nthe beginning of this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.41,0:10:29.09,Default,,0,0,0,,This judge is cheating.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.31,0:10:30.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew it!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.67,0:10:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got to step in, or Joey's\Nmind will be trapped here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.03,0:10:37.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, check out that light!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.69,0:10:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a second!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.09,0:10:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,That's Noah!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.23,0:10:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Master, what brings you\Nhere? Silence! Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.39,0:10:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Noah, it is him!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.33,0:10:56.83,Default,,0,0,0,,This is even worse than that\Nnever-ending virtual forest!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.27,0:10:58.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Mokuba!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.97,0:10:59.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.88,0:11:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.39,0:11:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Time out!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.71,0:11:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop the duel! Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.81,0:11:05.93,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.21,0:11:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Noah, you can't, sir. Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.05,0:11:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm only a few moves away from\Ntaking over this fool's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.49,0:11:15.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't deserve that prize, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.03,0:11:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Not after what you just pulled.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.99,0:11:19.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.90,0:11:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,So, he is a cheater.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.57,0:11:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Sad to say it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.41,0:11:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,The Honorable Judge Man\Nis nothing but a fraud
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.69,0:11:27.41,Default,,0,0,0,,who's been cheating you\Nfrom the very beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.49,0:11:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He's been using my virtual technology\Nto tamper with your dice rolls.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.93,0:11:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,How about I tamper with your face, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.21,0:11:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So-Called Man of Justice,\Nyou big fat fake?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.81,0:11:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,But, Noah, I couldn't risk losing this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.85,0:11:42.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, you must understand me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.95,0:11:46.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't take living in this virtual\Nprison for one moment longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.61,0:11:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It's torture.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.59,0:11:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Your excuses bore me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.45,0:11:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I brought you five into my world\Nwith the understanding that under
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.13,0:11:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,my leadership you would defeat\NSeto Kaiba and his little friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.37,0:12:01.61,Default,,0,0,0,,But if you cheat, I can't prove that\NI'm truly more deserving than him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.27,0:12:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Than me?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.45,0:12:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,More deserving of what?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.27,0:12:07.51,Default,,0,0,0,,For years I've lived in Seto's shadow,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.79,0:12:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,always trying to prove\Nthat I'm the better one.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.49,0:12:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I should be the president\Nof Kaiba Corp., not him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.29,0:12:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's about time\NI've proven to Gozaburo
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.45,0:12:17.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba that he should have\Nleft the company to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.05,0:12:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.96,0:12:24.49,Default,,0,0,0,,But my stepfather, Gozaburo, has been\Nmissing without a trace for over five years!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.11,0:12:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And why would Noah want to\Nprove something to him anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.79,0:12:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,This kid is not who he seems to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.47,0:12:32.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But who is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.25,0:12:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.69,0:12:38.29,Default,,0,0,0,,If I may interrupt this little\Nquarrel for just a second,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.37,0:12:40.03,Default,,0,0,0,,the defendant would like to speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.11,0:12:44.05,Default,,0,0,0,,If Johnson plays by the rules,\NI may still be able to win this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.59,0:12:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, but this doesn't concern you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.43,0:12:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Johnson, it's time for me to do something\Nthat I should have done the day I met you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.47,0:12:55.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Noah, please don't! Yoo-hoo.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.03,0:12:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Look,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.67,0:13:02.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm willing to forgive Judge Gruesome as\Nlong as he agrees to duel fair and square.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.51,0:13:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Noah, if he wins, you still\Nget to prove your strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.53,0:13:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And if I win,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.93,0:13:10.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I get to prove that Joey\NWheeler doesn't sit back
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.17,0:13:13.01,Default,,0,0,0,,and let freaky-looking\Nfrauds get the best of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.09,0:13:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.21,0:13:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, good luck, and I hope you\Nunderstand what you just did.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.35,0:13:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The stakes of this duel still stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.65,0:13:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, sure beats the subway.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.89,0:13:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, let's do this thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.33,0:13:29.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You did hear Noah, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.63,0:13:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You lose, and I still get to\Nescape by taking control of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.03,0:13:36.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.63,0:13:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.54,0:13:42.46,Default,,0,0,0,,then I guess you are as foolish as you look\Nbecause you're about to lose everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.55,0:13:43.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.46,0:13:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and with your body under my jurisdiction,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.21,0:13:48.95,Default,,0,0,0,,your mind will be sentenced to wander this
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.03,0:13:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,cyber universe for all\Neternity without bail.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.79,0:13:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You got me shaking in\Nmy boots, Your Honor.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.67,0:13:56.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You're real tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.95,0:13:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's too bad you can't\Ncheat anymore, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.39,0:14:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Touché.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.41,0:14:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's finish this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.57,0:14:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, looky here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.13,0:14:11.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I think my luck is beginning\Nto change now. All right!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.99,0:14:15.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hot! Agreed, let me draw two cards. Sweet!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.87,0:14:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,These two bad boys right\Nhere are just what I need.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.43,0:14:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And now it's time to move my Deck Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.87,0:14:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Flameswordsman,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.78,0:14:28.22,Default,,0,0,0,,go to the center of the playing field so\NI can use you to attack this Creepazoid.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.31,0:14:31.66,Default,,0,0,0,,But first, I'll boost your\Npower with Burning Soul Sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.97,0:14:34.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.67,0:14:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You need to sacrifice a monster\Nfor Burning Soul Sword to work.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.97,0:14:42.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what makes you think I don't\Nknow how my own magic card works?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.17,0:14:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I have to sacrifice a monster,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.73,0:14:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,and then whichever creature's holding\Nthe soul sword gets more attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.25,0:14:52.66,Default,,0,0,0,,In this case, that's my flamed swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.99,0:14:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I stand corrected. However,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.15,0:14:57.55,Default,,0,0,0,,you seem to have forgotten\None major fact about
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.63,0:15:00.75,Default,,0,0,0,,your strategy that will\Nprove to be most unfortunate,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.87,0:15:01.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.78,0:15:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.75,0:15:07.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You have no monsters left to Sacrifice,\Nyou fool, so your plan won't work.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.57,0:15:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not through yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.39,0:15:21.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I still got this little number left.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.51,0:15:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,My arduous decision magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.71,0:15:26.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Talk about risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.23,0:15:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,If this doesn't work, he could lose the\Nentire duel to Johnson right now, Taya.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.85,0:15:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But how, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.91,0:15:37.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Playing that magic card allows Joey\Nto draw two more cards from his deck,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.71,0:15:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,and that's where things get tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.01,0:15:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Because then Johnson has to\Npick one of those two cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.43,0:15:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,If he chooses a monster,\NJoey can summon it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.07,0:15:48.36,Default,,0,0,0,,But if he chooses a magic or trap card,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.51,0:15:51.13,Default,,0,0,0,,it goes to the graveyard\Nand Joey's turn is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.21,0:15:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, your choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.57,0:15:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,If you haven't figured it out yet,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.77,0:15:58.89,Default,,0,0,0,,the outcome of this entire\Nduel depends on this one move.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.97,0:16:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And with Noah watching, you can't cheat,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.37,0:16:04.14,Default,,0,0,0,,which means our fate will\Nbe decided by chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.69,0:16:07.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Your fate was sealed the moment we met.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.87,0:16:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Just pick a card, Jansen, and\Nquit your stalling already.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.61,0:16:13.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not a tough choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.73,0:16:15.08,Default,,0,0,0,,There's only two cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.37,0:16:17.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, if you choose a monster,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.53,0:16:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I can sacrifice it to\Npower up my flame swordsman
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.41,0:16:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,and blast away the rest\Nof your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.07,0:16:25.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but if I choose a magic or trap card,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.71,0:16:28.89,Default,,0,0,0,,then your swordsman remains\Nweak, and I'll destroy it,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.03,0:16:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,thus winning the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.91,0:16:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.41,0:16:33.91,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you gonna do here?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.99,0:16:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Choose right or left hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.43,0:16:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The time is now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.35,0:16:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, Joey, stay tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.39,0:16:43.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Johnson is losing his cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.33,0:16:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll never be able to\Ncheat his way out of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.59,0:16:50.65,Default,,0,0,0,,That fool Wheeler is risking the\Nentire duel on a game of chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.09,0:16:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, pick a card already.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.31,0:16:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,All this suspense is driving me crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.73,0:17:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, if you can't take it, just\Nimagine how Joey feels right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.13,0:17:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.79,0:17:07.45,Default,,0,0,0,,The more you put it off,\Nthe harder it's going to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.53,0:17:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Just pick a car, Jansen.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.93,0:17:11.25,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.67,0:17:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'm waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.85,0:17:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I pick your left hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.83,0:17:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.47,0:17:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, really sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.37,0:17:24.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.85,0:17:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That's an old trick, but a good one.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.89,0:17:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,However, I won't be fooled\Nby your childish antics.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.77,0:17:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You asked me twice if I was sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.11,0:17:36.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Your hesitation proves\NI've made the right choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.19,0:17:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,If you say so.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.45,0:17:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I've spent years and years convincing\Npeople that lies were truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.51,0:17:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,so you have little\Nchance of outwitting me,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.83,0:17:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.87,0:17:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm positive I haven't picked your\Nmonster card, so this case is closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.65,0:17:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Judgment in favor of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.31,0:17:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, please, show me the\Ncard in your left hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.33,0:17:57.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, wait. Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.71,0:17:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, I changed my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.29,0:18:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The right hand, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.47,0:18:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That's gotta hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.87,0:18:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah! All right!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.55,0:18:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You chose my monster card\Nknown as Goblin Attack Force.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.51,0:18:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,So now,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.71,0:18:19.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm able to sacrifice my goblins and add\Ntheir attack points to my Deckmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.87,0:18:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Flame Swordsman, Thanks to the\Npowers of my burning soul sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.25,0:18:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, it's time for Flame Swordsman\Nto attack Dragonist, the Wicked Knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.77,0:18:47.69,Default,,0,0,0,,No, this can't be.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.01,0:18:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I never lose in the courtroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.53,0:18:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I once convinced a jury that a man who\Nwas terrified of water stole a boat.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.17,0:18:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I be fooled by some kid?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.01,0:19:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.57,0:19:06.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.49,0:19:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Who's the man?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.87,0:19:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Way to go, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.87,0:19:12.31,Default,,0,0,0,,That was awesome! Ha-ha! Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.29,0:19:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, we still have to\Ngo find everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.09,0:19:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, the other members of the Big\NFive might be dueling them right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.89,0:19:22.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you say dueling them?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.37,0:19:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Who's dueling?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.61,0:19:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,They want to duel us all, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.63,0:19:29.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone who's trapped here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.21,0:19:30.73,Default,,0,0,0,,We are all in this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.95,0:19:32.77,Default,,0,0,0,,All of us! Stop, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.99,0:19:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not fair!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.19,0:19:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Serenity's never dueled before! No!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.93,0:19:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll find her, Joey, and\Nwe'll make sure she's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.91,0:19:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.31,0:19:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get moving!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.19,0:19:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm coming, Serenity!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.13,0:19:46.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.04,0:19:47.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait for us!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.95,0:19:49.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Come back, Joey! Please!
